{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Phase 2 landing progress (Gerrit change 2360 — https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2360)\n\nThe approved option-(b) fix (AC1/AC2 mint-time warning + AC3 serve-degraded health signal) was already implemented on change 2360 by a prior session. Landing it (not re-implementing) required a rebase onto a grown origin/main, which surfaced two module-size-gate failures that had to be resolved before CI would go Verified +1:\n\n1. Rebase conflict in `_mcp_health.py` (origin/main added a startup-handshake subsystem adjacent to the opcert block) — resolved by keeping BOTH subsystems; `/health` now returns `{in_flight, store, handshake, opcert}`.\n2. Module-size cap (800 LOC, `.github/module-size-limit.txt`) tripped on TWO files after the rebase:\n   - `_mcp_health.py` (877) → extracted the 4 opcert-health symbols into new `src/rebar/_mcp_opcert_health.py` (115 LOC). `_mcp_health.py` now 789.\n   - `_opcert_signing.py` (813) → extracted the same-environment verify subsystem (`_opcert_subject_binding_error`, `_required_environment`, `_pinned_environment_keys`, `_opcert_trust_root`, `verify_opcert_record`) into new `src/rebar/_opcert_verify.py` (340 LOC) along the existing mint/verify call-graph seam (mint never calls verify). `_opcert_signing.py` now 500. `verify_opcert_record` is re-exported from `_opcert_signing` at end-of-file so the public import site stays stable; the back-imports of `opcert_principal`/`_opcert_own_public_keys` are lazy (function-local) so neither import order forms a cycle (both orderings verified).\n\nValidation (worktree venv): `make lint` clean (ruff check + format + module-size + complexity-baseline new=0/increased=0); mypy clean; held-out test `test_opcert_public_counterpart_guard_879b.py` 12/12 GREEN; regression sweep `-k \"mcp_health or opcert or handshake or trusted_env or health or signing\"` = 484 passed / 6 skipped. Mutation proof re-run after the split: neuter the AC1/AC2 mint guard → 2 RED; force `opcert_signer_degraded`→False → 3 RED (5 RED total); restored → GREEN.\n\nPushed as patchset 7 (Change-Id Ied36e466…, `rebar-ticket:` trailer + DCO preserved). Awaiting LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1 before Submit; ticket stays in_progress until the change is Verified +1/merged."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788024412585409178,"uuid":"0b8c74df-b646-491a-b5db-253e21ca57b5"}